      "id": "errors/sceneIV_5.3/p@75236",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "DROMIO OF SYRACUSE.\nNo? Why, ’tis a plain case: he that went like a bass-viol in a case of leather; the man, sir, that, when gentlemen are tired, gives them a sob, and ’rests them; he, sir, that takes pity on decayed men and gives them suits of durance; he that sets up his rest to do more exploits with his mace than a morris-pike.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
