      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "DROMIO OF SYRACUSE.\nNay, she is worse, she is the devil’s dam; and here she comes in the habit of a light wench, and thereof comes that the wenches say “God damn me”, that’s as much to say, “God make me a light wench.” It is written they appear to men like angels of light. Light is an effect of fire, and fire will burn; ergo, light wenches will burn. Come not near her.",
